ttempt-07 R2)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > a cURL import's conversion report shows with its draft whether the result or the selecting snapshot arrives first; later selections stay protected (attempt-08 R2)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > a cURL import's conversion report shows when the result arrives before the selecting snapshot (attempt-08 R2)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > typing while an environment or schema save is pending is kept: the reply brings the revision, the next Save sends the newer text (attempt-08 R1)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > returning to an edited request after its editor unmounted reloads it from the core: the protected fields come back, never the old snapshot (attempt-09 R1)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > a superseded environment or schema open cannot replace the current editor or its typing: a newer selection, a new resource or Close retires it (attempt-09 R2)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > reads the preview for Variables and Preview, and the Collection chip’s menu opens the tools sheet, refreshes and closes the collection\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > creates a request draft from + and shows it new; a tab with edits the core could not protect closes only after the operator chooses to discard them\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > re-opens the selected request when the same collection is closed and opened again: following its selection is scoped to the open collection\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > replacing one collection directly with another collection id that selects the same request id loads the new collection’s document, never shows the old fields under it, and ignores the old collection’s late reply (attempt-03 R1)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > replacing one collection directly with the same collection id in a differently named folder that selects the same request id loads the new collection’s document, never shows the old fields under it, and ignores the old collection’s late reply (attempt-03 R1)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > replacing one collection directly with the same collection id and basename as Rust actually exposes for another parent folder that selects the same request id loads the new collection’s document, never shows the old fields under it, and ignores the old collection’s late reply (attempt-03 R1)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > draws nested folders as a hierarchy: a collapsed folder hides its whole subtree, a folder counts every request under it, and search still finds them\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > opens a collection tool from the keyboard; closing the sheet by Escape or its close control returns focus to the Collection chip, as the menu does on Escape (I8, T09)\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > a send from an already dirty request announces response metrics separately from its save state\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > a send from a new request announces response metrics without replacing \"New · not saved yet\"\n   ↓ C41 API Client board > shows the start panel with recents and no profile import when no collection is open, and the built-in collection opens from it\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  src/v2/workbench/api-client.test.tsx > C41 API Client board > uses only the restore warning for a core refusal after an undelivered load\nError: \u001b[2mexpect(\u001b[22m\u001b[31melement\u001b[39m\u001b[2m).not.toHaveTextContent()\u001b[22m\n\nExpected element not to have text content:\n\u001b[32m  That folder isn't empty\u001b[39m\nReceived:\n\u001b[31m  The preferred collection could not be opened. Restore its folder and try again, choose another collection, or open Strata Cloud Manager. That folder isn't empty and has no API Client collection (collection.toml). Choose an empty folder or a collection folder.Try again\u001b[39m\n ❯ src/v2/workbench/api-client.test.tsx:514:31\n    512|         await waitFor(() => expect(loads()).toBe(3))\n    513|         expect(warning()).toHaveTextContent('The preferred collection …\n    514|         expect(warning()).not.toHaveTextContent(\"That folder isn't emp…\n       |                               ^\n    515|         expect(warning()).not.toHaveTextContent('The desktop is busy')\n    516|         expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Try again' })).toBe…\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 46 skipped (47)\n   Start at  22:30:56\n   Duration  1.70s (transform 856ms, setup 52ms, collect 1.30s, tests 92ms, environment 119ms, prepare 39ms)\n\n11 fixture calls overflowed, PageDown reached lower call index 4, drawer content\nmoved and the Home anchor stayed fixed. Both images were accepted; fixture state,\nmodes and roots stayed unchanged. The [14-second supplement](../../evidence/P11/c47-scroll-supplement-01/supplement.json)\nis a separate actual execution, not an original capture rewritten.\n\nC48's first fix preserved failed preferred-collection recovery across navigation.\nIts original API 42, shell 29/Test Cases 16, Save/Send 20 and later focused 4/typecheck\nchecks keep their own exact source/timing bindings. A subsequent real\nApp/DesktopClient/native-adapter regression exposed initial/retry busy admission\nand rejected observation. The minimal API/store/test fix keeps every nonpositive\nLoad unresolved, stores only sanitized delivery messages in the existing scoped\nrecovery state, offers Start/Retry while loaded=false, and prevents automatic\nremount retries. Eight focused cases and typecheck passed. The malformed original\nbusy fixture produced a genuine generic failed-delivery result; its red 4 and\nfirst green 2-fail/6-pass outputs stay unchanged with that interpretation.\n\nNative03's PNG inspection then found a newly surfaced, misleading generic\ncore-refused folder detail. A final two-line message classification now displays\nshared text only for undelivered outcomes, preserves prior text on cancellation,\nand uses the accurate generic restore warning for core refusal. Failed/generation\nbehavior did not change. Four affected cases plus typecheck passed; the eight\nprior cases retain their actual earlier inputs instead of being rerun or called\nsame-source. The [final source selector chain](../../evidence/P11/retained-qa/c48-undelivered-02/supplement.json)\nretains all raw failures, exact diffs, snapshots and old broader source outcomes.\n\nThe source change is pinned to API Client, its tests and scoped store; App,\nRust, contracts, Save/Send controllers, JSON/URL/footer/tabs and styling remain\nunchanged by this last retry correction. The current evidence consumers and\nstanding/carry guards passed [20 affected pure Python tests](../../evidence/P11/review-carry-qa-01/record.json).\nEarlier 81 and the one parser follow-up retain original bindings; no broad\napplication/Rust/native/helper suite was relabelled current.\n\n## Final current fixture and native slice\n\n[Build08](../../evidence/P11/native-build-08-vm/receipt.json) passed on the final\n87:        executable_sha256: hex::encode(Sha256::digest(fs::read(\n90:        bundle_sha256: xtask::fingerprint::tree_hash(&bundle)?,\n//! Input fingerprints bound into review packets and receipts.\n//!\n//! * source: every tracked or untracked-but-not-ignored file (path, mode,\n//!   content or symlink target) plus the repository `.git/config`, minus a\n//!   narrow set of mutable evidence locations that are hashed separately.\n//! * dependencies: lockfiles, toolchain pin, the consumed immutable inputs\n//!   under `.inputs/`, and the resolved build-tool identities.\n//! * build_flags: the subject's manifest entries, Tauri configuration and\n//!   capability files, target and fixture-feature policy.\n//! * evidence: the subject's committed evidence directory.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse crate::manifest::Manifest;\nuse crate::{Repo, Result, Subject, invalid, io_err, sha256_hex};\n\n/// Mutable locations excluded from the source fingerprint. Each is hashed\n/// independently (evidence fingerprint, receipts) so exclusion cannot hide\n/// application sources, lockfiles, tests or configuration.\npub const SOURCE_EXCLUSIONS: [&str; 3] = [\n    \"docs/planning/status.md\",\n    \"docs/planning/reviews/\",\n    \"docs/planning/evidence/\",\n];\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct Fingerprints {\n    pub source: String,\n    pub dependencies: String,\n    pub build_flags: String,\n    pub evidence: String,\n}\n\n/// One entry of the source inventory.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct FileEntry {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub mode: String,\n    pub sha256: String,\n}\n\npub fn is_excluded(path: &str) -> bool {\n    SOURCE_EXCLUSIONS.iter().any(|excluded| {\n        if excluded.ends_with('/') {\n            path.starts_with(excluded)\n        } else {\n            path == *excluded\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n/// Lists source files via git: tracked plus untracked files not ignored.\npub fn source_inventory(repo: &Repo) -> Result<Vec<FileEntry>> {\n    let output = Command::new(\"/usr/bin/git\")\n        .args([\n            \"ls-files\",\n            \"-z\",\n            \"--cached\",\n            \"--others\",\n            \"--exclude-standard\",\n        ])\n        .current_dir(repo.root())\n        .env_clear()\n        .env(\"PATH\", \"/usr/bin:/bin\")\n        .env(\"HOME\", std::env::var(\"HOME\").unwrap_or_default())\n        .output()\n        .map_err(io_err(repo.root()))?;\n    if !output.status.success() {\n        return Err(invalid(\"git ls-files failed\"));\n    }\n    let mut paths: Vec<String> = output\n        .stdout\n        .split(|b| *b == 0)\n        .filter(|p| !p.is_empty())\n        .map(|p| String::from_utf8_lossy(p).into_owned())\n        .filter(|p| !is_excluded(p))\n        .collect();\n    paths.sort();\n    paths.dedup();\n    let mut entries = Vec::with_capacity(paths.len() + 1);\n    for path in paths {\n        entries.push(file_entry(repo.root(), &path)?);\n    }\n    entries.push(file_entry(repo.root(), \".git/config\")?);\n    Ok(entries)\n}\n\nfn file_entry(root: &Path, relative: &str) -> Result<FileEntry> {\n    let full = root.join(relative);\n    let Ok(meta) = std::fs::symlink_metadata(&full) else {\n        return Ok(FileEntry {\n            path: relative.to_owned(),\n            mode: \"deleted\".to_owned(),\n            sha256: String::new(),\n        });\n    };\n    if meta.file_type().is_symlink() {\n        let target = std::fs::read_link(&full).map_err(io_err(&full))?;\n        return Ok(FileEntry {\n            path: relative.to_owned(),\n            mode: \"symlink\".to_owned(),\n            sha256: sha256_hex(target.as_os_str().as_encoded_bytes()),\n        });\n    }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
